WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.570
Week 4: Identity, Origin, Numbers, and Time. state origin and profession exchange contact numbers tell dates and times

2
00:00:08.570 --> 00:00:20.727
Form and meaning. Applying the form. Use soy/eres/es/somos/son (from ser) for identity and origin, and pair cardinal numbers directly with the noun they count.

3
00:00:20.727 --> 00:00:40.542
Model set. Soy de Perú. Eres estudiante, ¿verdad? Es las tres de la tarde. Somos de la misma ciudad. Mi número tiene diez dígitos. I am from Peru. You are a student, right? It is three in the afternoon. We are from the same city. My number has ten digits.

4
00:00:40.542 --> 00:00:50.672
Contrastive practice. Change the person, time, number, or level of formality in each model. Preserve the communicative purpose while the grammar changes.

5
00:00:50.672 --> 00:01:03.533
Production check. Say one original sentence for each function: state origin and profession; exchange contact numbers; tell dates and times. Then write it and compare the spoken and written forms.

6
00:01:03.533 --> 00:01:24.073
Model language. Soy de Perú. — I am from Peru. Eres estudiante, ¿verdad? — You are a student, right? Es las tres de la tarde. — It is three in the afternoon. Somos de la misma ciudad. — We are from the same city. Mi número tiene diez dígitos. — My number has ten digits.

7
00:01:24.073 --> 00:01:33.822
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
